[12:29] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'wrong order. You end up with a bash script that breaks constantly. &gt;&gt; [clears throat] &gt;&gt; Docker Compose solves this by letting you describe your entire application in a single YAML file and bring everything up with one command. Before we look at'

[12:41] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'the full file, here is a simple way to think about it. Each service in your application runs as one container. The Compose file is a blueprint of your entire application. It describes how all those containers should run and interact'

[12:54] [scene:ui]
VISUAL: `compose.yaml` code for a three-tier application (db, api, frontend services) with explanations for each service.
